{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1820","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. JoJo's Incredible Adventures"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Did you think there was going to be a JoJo legend here? But no, that was me, Dio!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given a binary string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$, consisting of characters "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let's build a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"square"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" table of size $$$n \\times n$$$, consisting of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" characters as follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first row of the table write the original string $$$s$$$. In the second row of the table write "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cyclic shift"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the string $$$s$$$ by one to the right. In the third row of the table, write the cyclic shift of line $$$s$$$ by two to the right. And so on. Thus, the row with number $$$k$$$ will contain a cyclic shift of string $$$s$$$ by $$$k$$$ to the right. The rows "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"are numbered from $$$0$$$ to $$$n - 1$$$ top-to-bottom"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the resulting table we need to find the rectangle consisting only of ones that has the largest area."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We call a rectangle the set of all cells $$$(i, j)$$$ in the table, such that $$$x_1 \\le i \\le x_2$$$ and $$$y_1 \\le j \\le y_2$$$ for some integers $$$0 \\le x_1 \\le x_2 \\lt n$$$ and $$$0 \\le y_1 \\le y_2 \\lt n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Recall that the cyclic shift of string $$$s$$$ by $$$k$$$ to the right is the string $$$s_{n-k+1} \\ldots s_n s_1 s_2 \\ldots s_{n-k}$$$. For example, the cyclic shift of the string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01011"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" by $$$0$$$ to the right is the string itself \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01011"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", its cyclic shift by $$$3$$$ to the right is the string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01101"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test consists of multiple test cases. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 2 \\cdot 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases. The description of test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first and the only line of each test case contains a single binary string $$$s$$$ ($$$1 \\le \\lvert s \\rvert \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$), consisting of characters "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of string lengths $$$|s|$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer — the maximum area of a rectangle consisting only of ones. If there is no such rectangle, output $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n0\n1\n101\n011110\n101010\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n1\n2\n6\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, there is a table $$$1 \\times 1$$$ consisting of a single character "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", so there are no rectangles consisting of ones, and the answer is $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, there is a table $$$1 \\times 1$$$, consisting of a single character "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", so the answer is $$$1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, there is a table:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"chil